'' RUN: 'swap' over a 'string * N' passes the TAGGED length and fill -1 for that side.
'' The tag was truncated to a plain N, so the runtime took each side for a 'zstring * N':
'' the padding came back as a NUL and stale bytes and the copy ran into the next local.
'' Output identical to fbc-modern's, guard variables included.
'' TEST: cli
'' ARGS: -target windows-x86_64 tests/codegen/src/swap-fixed-str.bas -o tests/codegen/swapfixstr.exe
'' ENV: TIKO_LIBPATH=build/obj/rtlib/windows-x86_64
'' EXPECT-EXIT: 0
'' RUN: tests/codegen/swapfixstr.exe
'' EXPECT-RUN-EXIT: 0
'' EXPECT-RUN-OUT: [1234][abcd    ] 1 2 3
'' EXPECT-RUN-OUT: [abcd    ][str     ] 8
'' EXPECT-RUN-OUT: [1234][zz34] 1 2 3
